      "description": "Traigh Bhan Lagain Although the scene looks almost Mediterranean, I was walking briskly wearing a down jacket against the cold - the sunshine was courtesy of a high pressure area which meant clear night skies and a frost, and this was still before nine in the morning. The south part of Traigh Bhan Lagain behind the photographer is sandy, but much visited by cattle. Beyond a small headland the beach starts to become more bouldery and has no sand left beyond the point where the small stream of Sruthan a'Mhuilinn enters the loch at the right of the photo.\nThe peak in the distance is Beinn nan Gobhar, whilst, just visible poking out of the trees on the right, is Moy Castle, comprehensively wrapped in scaffolding for a lottery-funded restoration project.",
      "dateCreated": "2010-03-09",
